  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY NIGHT THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 209 PM CDT Mon Sep 14 2026\n\nOn a broad scale, Iowa will reside in generally fast flow around mid-\nlevel high pressure over the Deep South/Southeastern US, which will \nmigrate slowly back to the west by week's end. In this fast flow, \nthere will be a few shortwave troughs that pass through along with \nfragmented vorticity pieces, which will interface with a surface and \nelevated boundary draped across the region if not the state at \ntimes. The pattern is thus conducive to additional rounds of \nrainfall on what will be increasingly saturated soil and thus \nincreased risk of flash flooding with each successive round of rain. \nThis rainfall will route into waterways and lead to increasing river \nlevels with additional details in the hydrology discussion\nbelow.",
